Proposed v1 compliance core, shared by every job (Kano must-be):
- (M1) per-call category classifier plus in-call promotion/solicitation fence;
- (M2) series/CLI routing, A2P declaration export and number health;
- (M4) tenant-wide opt-out/suppression with attempt caps;
- (M6) DPDP notice, recording disclosure, retention and India residency;
- non-removable AI disclosure.
Performance tier: a calling-window engine keyed by category and sector. Deferred with pre-sale: the consent/inquiry ledger. Never market NCPR scrubbing as a feature: on 140 the operator scrubs.

Indian vendors' compliance docs against primary text:
- 0 of 3 mention the Third Amendment, A2P pre-declaration (due ~2026-11-18) or 1601;
- 2 of 3 state TRAI hours as 9 AM-9 PM (Bolna for all calls; Exotel for promotional), against the primary 10:00 start, and neither separates service calls, which have no band;
- Exotel says 'voice calls do not require DLT', calls a telco disincentive a sender penalty, and classes surveys/feedback as UCC;
- all 3 put compliance on the buyer.

RBI/2026-27/230 (NBFC RBC Third Amendment Directions, effective 2027-01-01), read in primary:
- contact only 08:00-19:00;
- call time and count logs;
- two-way recordings kept 6 months, borrower told;
- excessive or out-of-hours calling deemed harsh;
- grievance officer on every recovery communication;
- IIBF-certified recovery agents;
- explicit TCCCPR compliance (100AB).
100A extends these to normal-course collection only 'wherever explicitly specified'.

Tool findings.
REA 6.7.0:
- analyze-web-bundle hung (no output, killed at 300 s and 420 s) on a proxied headless-Chromium target;
- capture-browser-scenario launch mode has no proxy option, so navigation failed;
- connect mode to our own CDP Chromium worked (115 script URLs).
TLS: trai.gov.in (emSign root) and egazette.gov.in (missing Let's Encrypt YR1 intermediate) verify with Mozilla roots plus the published YR1 chain, with no verification disabled.
